<article class="env-lemma" id="0C5B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C5B">Lemma <span data-tag="0C5B">53.20.4</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be at-worst-nodal of relative dimension $1$. Then the same is true for any base change of $f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because the base change of a syntomic morphism is syntomic (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01UI" data-tag="01UI">29.31.4</a>), the base change of a morphism of relative dimension $1$ has relative dimension $1$ (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02NK" data-tag="02NK">29.30.2</a>), the formation of $\text{Sing}(f)$ commutes with base change (Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C3I" data-tag="0C3I">31.10.1</a>), and the base change of an unramified morphism is unramified (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02GA" data-tag="02GA">29.36.5</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>